Campfire wasm patch 0111: export wallet data in pages (issue #55, after 0110).

storage::ExportDataToJson (wasm patch 0110) builds the whole wallet data file as one
JSON tree and one string. The WebAssembly wallet runs in a fixed 100 MB heap
(INITIAL_MEMORY=100MB, ALLOW_MEMORY_GROWTH=0), so a wallet with a long history runs
it out of memory and the engine aborts for the page. Measured on 2026-10-11 with the
0110 build: an export of 7.5 MB worked, one of 10 MB aborted ("Cannot enlarge memory
arrays ... OOM"); the LightWallet test wallet's export is 17 MB (920 transactions,
1396 addresses). The web wallet therefore refuses an export it estimates above 6 MB.

This adds storage::ExportDataPageToJson(db, firstTx, maxBytes, nextTx): the same
transactions, the same skipping rules (deleted ones, ones without type or create
time) and the same fields as ExportTransactionsToJson, from the firstTx-th
exportable transaction until about maxBytes of JSON; page 0 also carries
OwnAddresses and Contacts. Parameters are grouped by pointer, not copied. And
WasmWalletClient.exportDataPage(firstTx, maxBytes, cb) -> cb(json, next) on the
main thread, next = -1 after the last page, cb(null, -1) on failure, held and
dropped like the 0110 callbacks.

The web wallet uses it when it is there (WalletSession.exportDataPages, joined by
lib/wallet_data.js joinPages into BEAM's usual file) and falls back to 0110 with the
size check otherwise. Not built by the worker: wallet_db.cpp and wasmclient.cpp
were only syntax-checked (native clang for wallet_db.cpp, emsdk clang for
wasmclient.cpp, -fsyntax-only, before and after the change).

